  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: \n\nUpper pattern continues to be quiet, and looks to remain quiet \nthrough Sunday, as models show a very weak and broad scale flow \nover the west, punctuated by a shallow trough over southern NV, \nand the lower Colorado river valley, and by weak riding over \nnorthern NV and ID. This flow setup looks to keep Nevada dry for \nthe next several days, however with the westerly Jet just to the \nnorth, models continue to show the pressure gradient over northern\nNevada tightening over recent runs. This will keep elevated fire \nweather conditions as westerly winds of 10 MPH to 20 MPH with \ngusts up to 35 MPH will possible over northern Humboldt and Elko \ncounties through Saturday. Elsewhere winds will be lighter out of \nthe W-SW at 5 to 15 MPH with gusts up to 25 MPH possible. Sunday \nthe stronger winds shift into central Nevada as a pacific trough \napproaches, shifting elevated to near critical fire weather \nconcerns into White Pine county. Monday, models show that northern\nstream upper level trough moving through Nevada, The GFS and \nECMWF continue to trend farther south with the track of the trough\nwith the trough with this system, while continuing to depict a \nfast moving system with not much moisture for Nevada, however this\ntrough will tap into tropical moisture from Hurricane Polo, just \nnot until it departs NV. There will still be a 10% to 40% chance \nfor light isolated showers accompanying trough passage Monday \nafternoon and evening, however the best chances at seeing rain \nwill be across central Nevada. Tuesday and Wednesday shortwave \nridging returns bringing another period of quiet weather \nconditions back to the Silver State. Model agreement dissipates \nThursday, as the GFS favors a zonal flow pattern over the west, \nwhile the ECMWF wants to build a strong long wave ridge over the \nsouthwestern US. Temperature wise Highs peak Friday afternoon with\ntemperatures in the mid to upper 80s. Saturday through Tuesday a \ncooling trend will see temperatures falling into the mid 70s for \nhighs. Wednesday will see another warming trend to finish out the \nweek with highs returning to the mid 80s. Lows will range in the \nmid to upper 40s for the first half of the forecast period, \ncooling into the mid to upper 30s by middle of next week.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \n\nThere is high confidence in a much drier pattern lasting through \nSunday of next week.\n\nThere is low confidence in the potential for a 10% to 40% chance \nfor isolated showers across Nevada as an upper trough passes \nthrough Monday of next week.\n\nThere is moderate confidence in the return of upper level ridging\nfor the middle of next week restoring quiet and dry pattern over \nNevada.",
